  "solution": {
    "notes": [
      "The implementations use a mutable character buffer, so O(n) storage is used."
    ],
    "approach": "Traverse the string in steps of 2k and reverse the first k characters of each block. Limit the reversal endpoint to the string length for the final partial block.",
    "editorial": {
      "better": {
        "complexity": "O(n) time and O(n) mutable-buffer space.",
        "description": "Use two pointers to reverse the required prefix inside each 2k block."
      },
      "optimal": {
        "complexity": "O(n) time and O(n) mutable-buffer space.",
        "description": "Scan block starts in increments of 2k and reverse the range from start to min(start+k, n). This directly handles both final-block cases."
      },
      "bruteForce": {
        "complexity": "O(n) time and O(n) extra space.",
        "description": "Process each 2k block independently, reverse its first k characters, or all remaining characters when fewer than k remain, and concatenate the blocks."
      }
    },
    "timeComplexity": "O(n)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(n)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nchar* reverseStr(char* s, int k) {\n    int n = (int)strlen(s);\n    for (int start = 0; start < n; start += 2 * k) {\n        int left = start;\n        int right = start + k - 1;\n        if (right >= n) right = n - 1;\n        while (left < right) {\n            char temp = s[left];\n            s[left] = s[right];\n            s[right] = temp;\n            left++;\n            right--;\n        }\n    }\n    return s;\n}",
      "C++": "class Solution {\npublic:\n    string reverseStr(string s, int k) {\n        for (int start = 0; start < (int)s.size(); start += 2 * k) {\n            int left = start;\n            int right = min(start + k - 1, (int)s.size() - 1);\n            while (left < right) {\n                swap(s[left], s[right]);\n                left++;\n                right--;\n            }\n        }\n        return s;\n    }\n};",
      "Java": "class Solution {\n    public String reverseStr(String s, int k) {\n        char[] a = s.toCharArray();\n        for (int start = 0; start < a.length; start += 2 * k) {\n            int left = start;\n            int right = Math.min(start + k - 1, a.length - 1);\n            while (left < right) {\n                char temp = a[left];\n                a[left] = a[right];\n                a[right] = temp;\n                left++;\n                right--;\n            }\n        }\n        return new String(a);\n    }\n}",
      "Python3": "import sys, json\n\nclass Solution:\n    def reverseStr(self, s: str, k: int) -> str:\n        a = list(s)\n        for start in range(0, len(a), 2 * k):\n            end = min(start + k, len(a))\n            a[start:end] = reversed(a[start:end])\n        return \"\".join(a)",
      "JavaScript": "'use strict';\n\nfunction reverseStr(s, k) {\n    const a = s.split('');\n    for (let start = 0; start < a.length; start += 2 * k) {\n        let left = start;\n        let right = Math.min(start + k - 1, a.length - 1);\n        while (left < right) {\n            [a[left], a[right]] = [a[right], a[left]];\n            left++;\n            right--;\n        }\n    }\n    return a.join('');\n}\n\nconst [s, k] = JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync(0, 'utf8'));\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(reverseStr(s, k)));"
    }
  },
